{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Live detection A/B (AC: efficacy, not just wording). Scratch ticket d67d-8167-86b5-446c carries a plan whose ONLY compaction trigger is a GitHub Actions schedule ('The workflow is the trigger: nothing else invokes compaction'), with no operation-linked or in-process fallback.\n\n- PRE-change rubric (git show HEAD:.rebar/prompts/plan-review-project-portability.md): 0 project.portability findings. The single undifferentiated 'CI' matrix cell left the no-CI-provider shape unnameable, so the reviewer stayed silent — the exact gap this ticket closes.\n- POST-change rubric: 1 project.portability finding, citing the sole-trigger sentence and naming both alternate shapes: 'A target project hosted on GitLab CI (or a self-hosted/BSD server running rebar as a library/MCP): .github/workflows/compact-store.yml never executes, so compaction never runs and the store log grows unbounded' and 'rebar consumed as a Python library on a developer workstation with no GitHub Actions: same never-fires no-op.'\n\nSame ticket text, same model, same region; only the rubric differed. The finding landed advisory rather than blocking on this scratch plan, which is Pass-3 disposition and not part of this ticket's scope — the criterion detecting the case at all is what changed."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786620711576152001,"uuid":"cb49aafa-a8bc-4aad-9474-c7ebbf926740"}